Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_US_CENSUS_PLACES.PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA  
  • "place_name": text filter to pick the Philadelphia record.  
  • "place_geom": polygon of each place – boundaries used with ST_CONTAINS.  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP_CENSUS_PLACES.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS  
  • "geometry": WKB point geometry of every OSM point – used for distance and containment.  
  • "all_tags": VARIANT array where the OSM key/value pairs live; look for objects whose key = 'amenity' and the value ∈ ('library','place_of_worship','community_centre','community center').  
  • "osm_id", "osm_version", "osm_timestamp": ids / time‐stamps useful for inspection.  

Extra columns that may help  
• "feature_type" (in PLANET_FEATURES; not vitally needed for points).  
• "internal_point_geom" and "internal_point_lat/lon": quick sanity check of Philadelphia centroid.  

Typical filtering conditions you will use  
1. In PLACES_PENNSYLVANIA  
   "place_name" ILIKE '%Philadelphia%'  

2. In PLANET_FEATURES_POINTS (after flattening "all_tags")  
   f.value:"key"::STRING = 'amenity'  
   and f.value:"value"::STRING ILIKE ANY ('%library%','%place%worship%','%community%centre%','%community%center%')  

3. Spatial relationship  
   ST_CONTAINS( ST_GEOMFROMWKB(p."place_geom"), ST_GEOMFROMWKB(pt."geometry") )  

